.TH REBELLION 1 "2026" "rebellion 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rebellion \- a Firecrawl-style web scraper that outputs clean Markdown
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rebellion
.I command
.I url
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rebellion
fetches web pages and converts them to clean Markdown plus structured
metadata and links. It has an HTTP engine (libcurl) and a headless Chromium
engine driven over the DevTools Protocol; an
.B auto
mode uses HTTP first and escalates to the browser when a page looks
JavaScript-gated. Legacy encodings (ISO-8859-1/15, Windows-1252) are detected
and converted to UTF-8.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B scrape \fIurl\fR
Fetch a single URL and emit Markdown (or JSON).
.TP
.B crawl \fIurl\fR
Crawl within a site (breadth-first) following links.
.TP
.B map \fIurl\fR
Quickly discover URLs from the site's sitemap(s) and homepage links.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-json
Emit JSON instead of Markdown.
.TP
.BR \-\-output ", " \-o " " \fIfile\fR
Write output to a file.
.TP
.B \-\-engine \fImode\fR
Rendering engine: \fBhttp\fR, \fBbrowser\fR, or \fBauto\fR (default).
.TP
.BR \-\-http ", " \-\-browser
Shorthands for \-\-engine.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-robots
Do not consult robots.txt. Use only where you have permission.
.TP
.B \-\-allow\-private
Allow scraping loopback/private/internal hosts (the SSRF guard blocks them by
default).
.TP
.B \-\-full\-page\-content
Keep the whole page instead of just the main content.
.TP
.B \-\-timeout \fIms\fR
Per-request timeout (default 30000).
.TP
.B \-\-delay \fIms\fR
Minimum delay between hits to one host.
.TP
.B \-\-screenshot \fIfile\fR
Save a PNG screenshot (implies the browser engine).
.TP
.B \-\-full\-page
Screenshot the whole page instead of the viewport.
.TP
.B \-\-proxy \fIurl\fR
Proxy URL (e.g. \fBhttp://user:pass@host:3128\fR or \fBsocks5h://host:1080\fR).
Repeat to build a rotating pool; overrides any proxy from the environment.
.TP
.B \-\-proxy\-strategy \fIs\fR
How to pick from the pool: \fBround\-robin\fR (default), \fBrandom\fR, or
\fBsticky\fR (same proxy per target host).
.TP
.B \-\-profile \fIdir\fR
Persistent browser profile directory. Cookies and logins are kept across
runs, so a session can reuse an authenticated profile.
.TP
.BR \-\-verbose ", " \-v
Log progress to stderr.
.SH "BROWSER ACTIONS"
For \fBscrape\fR, these run in order against a live headless browser before the
page is captured (they imply the browser engine):
.TP
.B \-\-wait\-for \fIselector\fR
Wait until a CSS selector appears.
.TP
.B \-\-click \fIselector\fR
Click the first matching element.
.TP
.B \-\-fill \fIselector=value\fR
Type a value into a form field.
.TP
.B \-\-submit \fIselector\fR
Submit a form (or the field's/button's form).
.TP
.B \-\-scroll\-bottom
Scroll to the bottom of the page (to trigger lazy loading).
.TP
.B \-\-wait \fIms\fR
Pause for the given number of milliseconds.
.SH "CRAWL OPTIONS"
.TP
.B \-\-limit \fIn\fR
Maximum pages to fetch (default 50).
.TP
.B \-\-depth \fIn\fR
Maximum link depth from the seed (default 2).
.TP
.B \-\-any\-host
Follow links off the seed's site.
.TP
.BR \-\-include ", " \-\-exclude " " \fIregex\fR
Only follow / skip URLs matching a POSIX extended regular expression.
.TP
.B \-\-out\-dir \fIdir\fR
Write one file per crawled page.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
A scrape, crawl, or map failed.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid command-line usage.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
rebellion scrape https://www.vr.de
rebellion scrape https://www.mediamarkt.de --browser
rebellion crawl https://example.de --limit 25 --out-dir ./out
rebellion map https://example.de
.fi
.SH "RESPONSIBLE USE"
rebellion respects robots.txt by default, honors Crawl-delay, and rate-limits
per host. Respect each site's terms of service, copyright, and applicable law
(including the GDPR for personal data). You are responsible for how you use it.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
Project documentation and source: see the bundled README and docs/ARCHITECTURE.md.
